mod backend.compiler.statements.branches;

/**
 * BRANCHES: statements that take one of several ways
 *
 *      if(n > 0) { ... } else if(n < 0) { ... } else { ... }
 *
 *      when(month) {                       when(subject): each value is compared with the subject
 *          2 -> days = 28;
 *          4, 6, 9, 11 -> days = 30;
 *          else -> days = 31;
 *      }
 *
 *      when {                              when without a subject: each value is a condition
 *          n < 10 -> small();
 *          else -> large();
 *      }
 *
 * A CONDITION (doc/backend.md 7.12.1) is a plain number - 0 is false - or a
 * `bool` object, whose `value` is taken. Of the number classes only `bool`
 * is a condition by itself: `if(an_int)` is E0411, as in the C++ compiler.
 * The rule is `analyse_condition` (backend/compiler/expressions/values.sharp).
 *
 * The files of this package (module `backend.compiler.statements.branches`):
 *
 *      branches.sharp          this front door
 *      if_statement.sharp      if / else if / else
 *      when_statement.sharp    when: the subject, the clauses, the else
 *      when_tests.sharp        one value of a clause as a test: "subject == value" bound like the
 *                              operator `==` (E0616); the same value twice (W1020)
 *
 * This file is the package's front door: it only says what is where.
 */
